and grill</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Standard zones</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Blackmoor</strong></td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Murrells Inlet, Highway 707</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Gary Player design, public</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">None required</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">345 homes from the high $200,000s, plus Marcliffe villas</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">About $35/mo, the lowest verified golf-community fee here</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">No gate; standard zones</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Prince Creek / TPC</strong></td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">TPC Myrtle Beach, Tom Fazio, the only TPC in South Carolina, public play</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">None required</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Villages from the low $300,000s to $600,000s+</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Varies by village</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Gated enclaves inside; creek-adjacent lots need a flood check</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Dunes Club area</strong></td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Myrtle Beach north end, oceanfront</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Robert Trent Jones Sr., 1948; hosts the PGA Tour's Myrtle Beach Classic; essentially private</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Club membership separate from homeownership</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">From about $500K to oceanfront estates</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Older streets often have no mandatory HOA; verify per listing</td><td style="padding:.5rem .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);vertical-align:top">Oceanfront pockets can be VE or AE zones</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
 
 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The fine print</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What Myrtle Beach golf community buyers miss</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.8rem;margin:1.2rem 0 0;padding:0;max-width:760px"><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Transfer fees ride with the deed, not the listing.</strong> At Barefoot, a resale that carries a golf membership means a $2,750 transfer fee and a 60-day enrollment window after closing. Ask what obligations attach to the specific lot before you offer, not at the closing table.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The Intracoastal view can carry a flood premium.</strong> Waterway-adjacent pockets of Grande Dunes, Barefoot, and Arrowhead can sit in FEMA Zone AE, where lenders require flood insurance. The fairway lots a street inland often do not. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">coastal insurance guide</a> covers what that costs; we pull the flood zone on every golf lot we show.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">A public course means no membership obligation.</strong> Public-course communities like Blackmoor pair a Gary Player design with a $35 monthly HOA and no club dues at all. Clients of ours owned a home in Blackmoor, then sold it and bought in Seasons at Prince Creek West, a 55+ community a few minutes away. That side is covered on our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">55+ communities page</a>.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Second-home rules still apply on the fairway.</strong> A golf villa you use part-time is a second home or investment property to the county and the lender: the 6 percent tax rate, second-home loan occupancy rules, and rental restrictions all still run. The math is in our <a href="/buyers/second-home/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">second home guide</a> and <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax calculator</a>.</span></li></ul></div></section>
 
 <section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Match a Myrtle Beach golf community to how you play.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:600px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Tell us your budget, whether you want the club or just the course view, and how you feel about gates. We confirm the current membership terms, fees, and flood zones on every match, and our lending partner, BrickWood Mortgage, handles second-home and investment financing.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Find my golf community</a><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--brass-2);text-decoration:none;align-self:center">55+ communities →</a></div></div></section>
 
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Sources</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.45rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Where these numbers come from</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.55rem;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:720px;font-size:.88rem"><li style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><a href="https://www.visitmyrtlebeach.com/things-to-do/golf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">Visit Myrtle Beach: Grand Strand golf course count</a></li><li style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><a href="https://barefootgolf.com/membership/membership-frequently-asked-questions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">Barefoot Resort Golf: membership transfer fee and dues</a></li><li style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><a href="https://www.55places.com/south-carolina" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">Community price, HOA, and membership data via community and brokerage listings</a></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:1rem;max-width:720px">Verified July 2026. Community fees and figures change; we confirm current numbers with each community before you offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Myrtle Beach golf communities FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do you have to join the club to live in a Myrtle Beach golf community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Almost never. Membership is optional at Barefoot, Prestwick, Pawleys Plantation, and even private Wachesaw Plantation, though non-members there get no amenities since everything belongs to the club. Where the course is public, like Arrowhead, Wild Wing, Blackmoor, Legends, International Club, and TPC Myrtle Beach, there is no membership to join at all.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How many golf courses does Myrtle Beach have?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">More than 80 championship courses, per Visit Myrtle Beach's current figure. The 100-course number still quoted around the internet is outdated. The oldest is Pine Lakes International, opened 1927; the most famous is the Dunes Golf and Beach Club, a 1948 Robert Trent Jones Sr. design that hosts the PGA Tour's Myrtle Beach Classic.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is the Barefoot Resort golf transfer fee?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Resale buyers of Barefoot homes that carry a golf membership pay a $2,750 transfer fee to Barefoot Resort Golf Club, with enrollment required within 60 days of closing. Dues run $205 a month for golf and social access or $85 for social only, covering the Dye, Love, Fazio, and Norman courses.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is TPC Myrtle Beach private?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. It is the only TPC in South Carolina and it welcomes public play, which is rare for the brand. It anchors the Prince Creek master plan in Murrells Inlet, where villages range from the low $300,000s to the $600,000s and up, including the Seasons 55+ community.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which Myrtle Beach golf communities are gated with a guard?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Prestwick has a 24/7 staffed gate, Wachesaw Plantation runs 24-hour security, and Wachesaw East and Pawleys Plantation are gated. Grande Dunes and Barefoot are gated only in certain villages, and value communities like Blackmoor and Wild Wing are open.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is the cheapest golf community in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Legends' Turnberry Park condos at $150,000 to $215,000 and Arrowhead condos from about $175,000 are the verified low end for buying in. For houses, Blackmoor pairs a Gary Player course with roughly a $35 monthly HOA, the lowest fee we verified in any Grand Strand golf community.</p></div></div></section>
+<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Sources</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.45rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Where these numbers come from</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.55rem;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:720px;font-size:.88rem"><li style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><a href="https://www.visitmyrtlebeach.com/things-to-do/golf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">Visit Myrtle Beach: Grand Strand golf course count</a></li><li style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><a href="https://barefootgolf.com/membership/membership-frequently-asked-questions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">Barefoot Resort Golf: membership transfer fee and dues</a></li><li style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><a href="https://www.55places.com/south-carolina" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">Community price, HOA, and membership data via community and brokerage listings</a></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:1rem;max-width:720px">Verified July 2026. Community fees and figures change; we confirm current numbers with each community before you offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Myrtle Beach golf communities FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do you have to join the club to live in a Myrtle Beach golf community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Almost never. Membership is optional at Barefoot, Prestwick, Pawleys Plantation, and even private Wachesaw Plantation, though non-members there get no amenities since everything belongs to the club. Where the course is public, like Arrowhead, Wild Wing, Blackmoor, Legends, International Club, and TPC Myrtle Beach, there is no membership to join at all.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How many golf courses does Myrtle Beach have?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">More than 80 championship courses, per Visit Myrtle Beach's current figure. The 100-course number still quoted around the internet is outdated. The oldest is Pine Lakes International, opened 1927; the most famous is the Dunes Golf and Beach Club, a 1948 Robert Trent Jones Sr. design that hosts the PGA Tour's Myrtle Beach Classic.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is the Barefoot Resort golf transfer fee?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Resale buyers of Barefoot homes that carry a golf membership pay a $2,750 transfer fee to Barefoot Resort Golf Club, with enrollment required within 60 days of closing. Dues run $205 a month for golf and social access or $85 for social only, covering the Dye, Love, Fazio, and Norman courses.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is TPC Myrtle Beach private?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. It is the only TPC in South Carolina and it welcomes public play, which is rare for the brand. It anchors the Prince Creek master plan in Murrells Inlet, where villages range from the low $300,000s to the $600,000s and up, including the Seasons 55+ community.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which Myrtle Beach golf communities are gated with a guard?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Tidewater Plantation, Wachesaw Plantation, Willbrook Plantation and DeBordieu Colony have a guard gate or guard house. Grande Dunes and Barefoot Resort are gated only in some sections. Our <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to gated communities near Myrtle Beach</a> has the map.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is the cheapest golf community in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Legends' Turnberry Park condos at $150,000 to $215,000 and Arrowhead condos from about $175,000 are the verified low end for buying in. For houses, Blackmoor pairs a Gary Player course with roughly a $35 monthly HOA, the lowest fee we verified in any Grand Strand golf community.</p></div></div></section>
